From 7c8cf2547920e0e2ef9773a485b69249e9f55f99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LegendaryFire <tristan.balon@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:25:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Run Inkling 2's K-quant and Q5_0 experts (Bartowski's Q4_K_M)
 at speed

Only NVFP4 and Q8_0 experts had the prompt GEMM, the CPU decode path
and the pool: a GGUF with Q4_K / Q5_K / Q6_K gate-up and Q5_0 down
experts (bartowski's thinkingmachines_Inkling-2-Mini-Q4_K_M) read
prompts at 357 tok/s with every expert in VRAM and could not run with
experts in RAM at all. Now:

- the warp-specialized prompt GEMM (k_expert_ws) converts Q4_K, Q5_K,
  Q6_K and Q5_0 rows to FP16 as their formats define them (d sc q -
  dmin m with 6-bit scales and mins; Q5_K's fifth bits; Q6_K's 6-bit
  codes and scale a 16; Q5_0's (q - 16) d): a K-quant super-block a
  raw copy (Q5_K / Q6_K on 64-column tiles, so the buffers fit; Q6_K's
  2-byte aligned rows copied 16 bits at a time), Q5_0 two steps a
  copy; Q8_0 moves to it from k_expert_mma2 (two steps a copy; the
  16-byte copies only where every copy starts 16-aligned);
- a layer takes the GEMM with any of NVFP4 / Q8_0 / Q4_K / Q5_K / Q6_K
  gate-up and NVFP4 / Q8_0 / Q5_0 down, each projection by its type;
- the CPU's expert dots (scalar and AVX2) take Q4_K, Q5_K, Q6_K and
  Q5_0 (the K-quants' mins against the int8 codes' sums, as ggml's
  GPU kernels), so these experts run from RAM in the pool.

Checks: the GEMM's conversions agree with the generic grouped kernels
as the NVFP4 path does (~0.9%, the q8_1 activations' rounding); the
CPU dots against a double-precision dequantized reference (<2.4e-4)
and the GPU's kernels in the engine (~1.3e-7).

Bartowski's Q4_K_M, every expert in VRAM, 7K: prompt 357 -> 1708
tok/s (1907 at 1024-token chunks). In the pool at 512K (two cards, the
drafter): prompt 7K 1942, 60K 1685, 180K 1137 tok/s; decode 53.3,
48.6, 45.4 (UD-Q4_K_XL: 2020 / 2379 / 1893 and 62.2 / 55.3 / 54.7:
the larger file leaves fewer experts in VRAM). UD-Q4_K_XL's Q8_0
layers on the new path: prompt at 1024-token chunks 2004 -> 2077.
